  "lineage": "Interwar compositional movement (c.1920-1950) characterized by return to clear textures, balanced forms, and reference to pre-Romantic models (Bach, Haydn, Stravinsky himself looking back to his Russian-folk past), combined with extended chromatic and rhythmic vocabulary. Stravinsky's Pulcinella (1920), Octet (1923), and Symphony of Psalms (1930) are the canonical type-specimens. Distinguished from Romantic by neoclassicism's anti-emotional-excess aesthetic and from Second Viennese serialism by retention of tonal-modal centers.",
